    "# Recommendation System (NLP)\n",
    "\n",
    "## MovieLens\n",
    "\n",
    "MovieLens is the most widely used benchmark dataset in **recommender systems research**. For recommendation systems, MovieLens plays a role similar to what ImageNet played for computer vision: it provided a standardized dataset and evaluation framework that enabled rapid progress in the field.\n",
    "\n",
    "Created and maintained by the GroupLens Research at the University of Minnesota, MovieLens contains millions of movie ratings from real users and has been used in thousands of academic papers.\n",
    "\n",
    "It contains:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Users\n",
    "* Movies\n",
    "* Ratings\n",
    "* Tags\n",
    "* Timestamps\n",
    "* Metadata\n",
    "\n",
    "The core task is:\n",
    "\n",
    "> Predict what movies a user will like based on past behavior.\n",
    "\n",
    "Unlike ImageNet, which focuses on perception (\"What object is in this image?\"), MovieLens focuses on personalization:\n",
    "\n",
    "> \"What item should this user see next?\"\n",
    "\n",
    "### Historical Background\n",
    "\n",
    "The MovieLens website started in 1997 as an online movie recommendation service.\n",
    "\n",
    "Researchers realized they had accumulated a valuable dataset of:\n",
    "\n",
    "* User preferences\n",
    "* Explicit ratings\n",
    "* User-item interactions\n",
    "\n",
    "They released anonymized versions for research.\n",
    "\n",
    "Over time multiple versions emerged:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Dataset        | Ratings              |\n",
    "| -------------- | -------------------- |\n",
    "| MovieLens 100K | 100,000              |\n",
    "| MovieLens 1M   | 1 million            |\n",
    "| MovieLens 10M  | 10 million           |\n",
    "| MovieLens 20M  | 20 million           |\n",
    "| MovieLens 25M  | 25 million           |\n",
    "| Latest Full    | Continuously updated |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Dataset Architecture\n",
    "\n",
    "MovieLens is fundamentally a **user-item interaction matrix**.\n",
    "\n",
    "* Rows/Samples: 100,000 ratings\n",
    "* 943 users\n",
    "* 1,682 movies\n",
    "\n",
    "**Target Variable**\n",
    "\n",
    "* Typically Rating Prediction\n",
    "* Target rating Range: 0.5 – 5.0\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Ratings Table\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "| UserID | MovieID | Rating | Timestamp |\n",
    "| ------ | ------- | ------ | --------- |\n",
    "| 1      | 10      | 4.5    | 964982703 |\n",
    "| 1      | 25      | 5.0    | 964983815 |\n",
    "| 2      | 100     | 3.0    | 964985000 |\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Movies Table\n",
    "\n",
    "| MovieID | Title     | Genres            |\n",
    "| ------- | --------- | ----------------- |\n",
    "| 1       | Toy Story | Animation|Comedy  |\n",
    "| 2       | Jumanji   | Adventure|Fantasy |\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Tags Table\n",
    "\n",
    "| UserID | MovieID | Tag     |\n",
    "| ------ | ------- | ------- |\n",
    "| 15     | 50      | classic |\n",
    "| 20     | 100     | sci-fi  |\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Links Table\n",
    "\n",
    "Maps movies to external databases:\n",
    "\n",
    "* IMDb IDs\n",
    "* TMDb IDs\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Data Dictionary\n",
    "\n",
    "| Feature   | Data Type | Description      | Possible Values  | Missing | Importance |\n",
    "| --------- | --------- | ---------------- | ---------------- | ------- | ---------- |\n",
    "| userId    | Integer   | Unique user ID   | Positive integer | No      | Very High  |\n",
    "| movieId   | Integer   | Unique movie ID  | Positive integer | No      | Very High  |\n",
    "| rating    | Float     | User rating      | 0.5–5.0          | No      | Target     |\n",
    "| timestamp | Integer   | Rating timestamp | Unix time        | No      | High       |\n",
    "| title     | String    | Movie title      | Text             | Rare    | Medium     |\n",
    "| genres    | String    | Movie categories | Multiple genres  | No      | High       |\n",
    "| tag       | String    | User tags        | Text             | Yes     | Medium     |\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "### The User-Item Matrix\n",
    "\n",
    "The heart of MovieLens is:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "R_{u,i}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where:\n",
    "\n",
    "* $u$ = user\n",
    "* $i$ = item/movie\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "| User | Toy Story | Titanic | Matrix |\n",
    "| ---- | --------- | ------- | ------ |\n",
    "| U1   | 5         | ?       | 4      |\n",
    "| U2   | 3         | 5       | ?      |\n",
    "| U3   | ?         | 2       | 5      |\n",
    "\n",
    "Question marks are unknown ratings.\n",
    "\n",
    "The recommendation problem is:\n",
    "\n",
    "> Predict the missing values.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Problem MovieLens Solved\n",
    "\n",
    "Before MovieLens:\n",
    "\n",
    "* No standard recommendation benchmark\n",
    "* Small proprietary datasets\n",
    "* Difficult comparisons across papers\n",
    "\n",
    "Researchers could not fairly evaluate algorithms.\n",
    "\n",
    "MovieLens solved this by providing:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Standardization: Everyone used the same dataset.\n",
    "* Reproducibility: Results became comparable.\n",
    "* Scale: Millions of real user interactions.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Real-world behavior**\n",
    "\n",
    "Not synthetic data.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Types of Recommendation Problems\n",
    "\n",
    "MovieLens supports several recommendation tasks.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Rating Prediction\n",
    "\n",
    "Predict:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\hat{R}_{u,i}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "User has not watched Titanic.\n",
    "\n",
    "Predict:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "User 17 → Titanic = 4.7\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Top-N Recommendation\n",
    "\n",
    "Recommend:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Top 10 movies user is likely to enjoy\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Most modern systems use this.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Ranking\n",
    "\n",
    "* Sort movies by predicted relevance.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Personalized Search\n",
    "\n",
    "* Generate individualized ordering.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Classical Algorithms Developed on MovieLens\n",
    "\n",
    "#### User-Based Collaborative Filtering\n",
    "\n",
    "Idea: Find similar users.\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "User A likes:\n",
    "- Matrix\n",
    "- Terminator\n",
    "\n",
    "User B likes:\n",
    "- Matrix\n",
    "- Terminator\n",
    "- Alien\n",
    "\n",
    "Recommend Alien to A.\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Similarity Metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "Cosine similarity:\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\cos(\\theta)=\\frac{A\\cdot B}{|A||B|}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "Measures similarity between user rating vectors.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Item-Based Collaborative Filtering\n",
    "\n",
    "Instead of similar users:\n",
    "\n",
    "Find similar movies.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Users who liked Matrix\n",
    "also liked Terminator\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Recommend Terminator.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Matrix Factorization Revolution\n",
    "\n",
    "The biggest breakthrough on MovieLens was matrix factorization.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Motivation\n",
    "\n",
    "User-item matrix is sparse.\n",
    "```\n",
    "100,000 users × 10,000 movies\n",
    "```\n",
    "Possible ratings:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "10^9\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Observed ratings:\n",
    "\n",
    "Only a tiny fraction.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Matrix Factorization Architecture\n",
    "\n",
    "Decompose:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "R \\approx PQ^T\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Where:\n",
    "\n",
    "* P = user latent factors\n",
    "* Q = movie latent factors\n",
    "\n",
    "User latent vector:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "[\n",
    "    Action=0.9\n",
    "    Romance=0.2\n",
    "    SciFi=0.8\n",
    "]\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Movie latent vector:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "[\n",
    "    Action=0.8\n",
    "    Romance=0.1\n",
    "    SciFi=0.9\n",
    "]\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Dot product:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\hat{R}_{u,i}=P_u\\cdot Q_i\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "High score → recommend.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Netflix Prize Connection\n",
    "\n",
    "Netflix Prize transformed recommendation research.\n",
    "\n",
    "MovieLens became the primary academic benchmark for techniques developed during that era.\n",
    "\n",
    "Key innovations:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Matrix factorization\n",
    "* SVD\n",
    "* Regularization\n",
    "* Ensemble methods\n",
    "\n",
    "### Deep Learning Era\n",
    "\n",
    "MovieLens became the benchmark for neural recommenders.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Neural Collaborative Filtering (NCF)\n",
    "\n",
    "Architecture:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "User ID\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "Embedding\n",
    "\n",
    "Movie ID\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "Embedding\n",
    "\n",
    "Concatenate\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "MLP Layers\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "Prediction\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Embeddings\n",
    "\n",
    "Users and movies become dense vectors:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "User 17 → [0.12, -0.84, ...]\n",
    "Movie 25 → [0.45, 0.91, ...]\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "The network learns latent preferences.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Modern Architectures\n",
    "\n",
    "Used extensively on MovieLens:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Autoencoders\n",
    "* Neural Collaborative Filtering\n",
    "* Wide & Deep models\n",
    "* Transformers\n",
    "* Graph Neural Networks\n",
    "* Sequential recommenders\n",
    "\n",
    "### Evaluation Metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "#### RMSE\n",
    "\n",
    "Most famous MovieLens metric.\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "RMSE=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{N}\\sum(y-\\hat{y})^2}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Measures rating prediction accuracy.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### MAE\n",
    "\n",
    "Mean Absolute Error.\n",
    "\n",
    "* Precision@K: How many recommendations are relevant.\n",
    "* Recall@K: How many relevant items were retrieved.\n",
    "* NDCG: Measures ranking quality.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Dataset Characteristics\n",
    "\n",
    "MovieLens has several unique properties.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Explicit Feedback\n",
    "\n",
    "Users intentionally rate movies.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "5 stars\n",
    "4 stars\n",
    "3 stars\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "This differs from:\n",
    "\n",
    "* clicks\n",
    "* views\n",
    "* watch time\n",
    "\n",
    "which are implicit feedback.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Sparse Matrix\n",
    "\n",
    "Typically:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "More than 95% missing entries\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Sometimes >99%.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Long-Tail Distribution\n",
    "\n",
    "Few movies get many ratings.\n",
    "\n",
    "Most movies receive very few ratings.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Limitations of MovieLens\n",
    "\n",
    "Despite its importance, MovieLens has significant limitations.\n",
    "\n",
    "* Selection Bias\n",
    "    * Only active users rate movies.\n",
    "    * Dataset doesn't represent all viewers.\n",
    "* Explicit Feedback Bias  \n",
    "    * Real platforms mainly use:\n",
    "        * clicks\n",
    "        * watch duration\n",
    "        * purchases\n",
    "\n",
    "    MovieLens mostly uses ratings.\n",
    "* Small Scale by Modern Standards\n",
    "    * MovieLens 25M:`25 million interactions`\n",
    "    * Modern systems: `billions to trillions`\n",
    "* Domain Restriction: Only movies.\n",
    "    Modern recommenders need:\n",
    "    * music\n",
    "    * products\n",
    "    * ads\n",
    "    * social content\n",
    "    * videos\n",
    "* Static Dataset  \n",
    "    Real systems have:\n",
    "    * changing interests\n",
    "    * new users\n",
    "    * new items  \n",
    "    MovieLens snapshots are largely static.\n",
    "* Cold Start Problem Remains\n",
    "    * New user: No ratings\n",
    "    * New movie: No interactions  \n",
    "    Collaborative filtering struggles.\n",
    "* Missing Context  \n",
    "    MovieLens lacks many contextual signals:\n",
    "    * location\n",
    "    * weather\n",
    "    * mood\n",
    "    * device\n",
    "    * social influence  \n",
    "    Modern recommenders use these heavily.\n",
    "* Not Representative of Industry  \n",
    "    Real recommendation systems include:\n",
    "    * ranking\n",
    "    * retrieval\n",
    "    * candidate generation\n",
    "    * business constraints\n",
    "    * diversity optimization\n",
    "    * fairness objectives  \n",
    "    MovieLens simplifies these complexities.\n",
    "### Why MovieLens Is Still Important\n",
    "\n",
    "MovieLens remains valuable because it is:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Public\n",
    "* Clean\n",
    "* Well-documented\n",
    "* Reproducible\n",
    "* Easy to compare against prior work\n",
    "\n",
    "Researchers can quickly test new recommendation algorithms without access to proprietary industry data.\n",
    "\n",
    "### MovieLens' Legacy\n",
    "\n",
    "MovieLens enabled the development and evaluation of:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Collaborative Filtering\n",
    "* Matrix Factorization\n",
    "* SVD-based recommenders\n",
    "* Neural Collaborative Filtering\n",
    "* Deep recommendation systems\n",
    "* Graph-based recommenders\n",
    "* Transformer recommenders\n",
    "\n",
    "Its role in recommender systems is similar to:\n",
    "\n",
    "* ImageNet for computer vision\n",
    "* MNIST for early deep learning\n",
    "* GLUE for NLP benchmarking\n",
    "\n",
    "In short, MovieLens provided the standardized user–movie interaction data that allowed recommendation systems to evolve from simple nearest-neighbor methods to today's large-scale embedding, graph, and transformer-based recommendation architectures.\n",
