    "## Berlin-APC\n",
    "\n",
    "**Berlin-APC** is a publicly available dataset designed for **Automated Passenger Counting (APC)** in trains and public transportation systems. It was created by researchers from Technische Universität Berlin and collaborators to enable the development of AI systems that can count passengers **without violating privacy**. Unlike traditional CCTV datasets, Berlin-APC contains only low-resolution depth information from 3D sensors, making identification of individual passengers impossible while still allowing accurate counting.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why Was Berlin-APC Created?\n",
    "\n",
    "Public transport operators need accurate passenger counts for:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Capacity planning\n",
    "* Revenue sharing between operators\n",
    "* Timetable optimization\n",
    "* Fleet management\n",
    "* Crowd monitoring\n",
    "* Passenger information systems\n",
    "\n",
    "Traditional APC systems often use:\n",
    "\n",
    "* RGB cameras\n",
    "* Infrared sensors\n",
    "* Light barriers\n",
    "* Weight sensors\n",
    "\n",
    "However, RGB cameras raise serious privacy concerns because they record identifiable faces and personal information.\n",
    "\n",
    "The Berlin-APC project addresses this problem by using **3D LiDAR / Time-of-Flight (ToF) depth sensors** that capture only distance information rather than photographs. \n",
    "\n",
    "### Main Goal of the Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "The dataset is intended to train machine learning systems to estimate:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Boarding passengers** (people entering the train)\n",
    "2. **Alighting passengers** (people leaving the train)\n",
    "\n",
    "for each door-opening event.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Data Collection Environment\n",
    "\n",
    "The recordings were made:\n",
    "\n",
    "* In a regional train operating around Berlin\n",
    "* During normal passenger service\n",
    "* In 2017\n",
    "* Using overhead-mounted 3D LiDAR sensors above train doors\n",
    "* At 10 frames per second (fps) \n",
    "\n",
    "The sensor continuously recorded door areas whenever the train stopped and passengers moved through the doors.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Sensor Technology\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Time-of-Flight (ToF) Sensor\n",
    "\n",
    "Instead of taking normal photographs, the sensor measures distance.\n",
    "\n",
    "Each pixel stores:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Distance from sensor to object\n",
    "* Depth information only\n",
    "\n",
    "No color information exists.\n",
    "\n",
    "No facial features exist.\n",
    "\n",
    "No personal identity information exists.\n",
    "\n",
    "This makes the dataset highly privacy-preserving.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Data Resolution\n",
    "\n",
    "The original ToF sensor produced larger depth images.\n",
    "\n",
    "For publication:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Resolution reduced to **20 × 25 pixels**\n",
    "* Single channel (depth only)\n",
    "* Frame rate = **10 fps**\n",
    "\n",
    "Thus every frame contains only:\n",
    "\n",
    "20 × 25 = **500 depth values**\n",
    "\n",
    "compared with a normal camera image containing hundreds of thousands of RGB values.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Dataset Size\n",
    "\n",
    "Berlin-APC contains:\n",
    "\n",
    "* **12,956 video sequences**\n",
    "* Approximately **13,000 annotated recordings**\n",
    "* Around **26,243 boarding events**\n",
    "* Around **26,164 alighting events**\n",
    "\n",
    "This makes it one of the largest publicly available APC datasets based on depth sensing.\n",
    "\n",
    "### What Is a Sequence?\n",
    "\n",
    "A sequence corresponds to a complete door-opening cycle.\n",
    "\n",
    "Typical sequence:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Door closed\n",
    "2. Door opens\n",
    "3. Passengers board and/or leave\n",
    "4. Door closes\n",
    "\n",
    "One sequence may contain:\n",
    "\n",
    "* No passengers\n",
    "* One passenger\n",
    "* Multiple passengers\n",
    "* Crowded situations\n",
    "* Bicycles\n",
    "* Luggage\n",
    "* Sensor noise\n",
    "\n",
    "Each sequence has variable length. \n",
    "\n",
    "### Sequence Shape\n",
    "\n",
    "Every sequence has shape:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "(t, 20, 25)\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "where:\n",
    "\n",
    "* t = number of frames\n",
    "* 20 = image height\n",
    "* 25 = image width\n",
    "\n",
    "Examples:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "100 × 20 × 25\n",
    "250 × 20 × 25\n",
    "500 × 20 × 25\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "depending on how long the door remained open.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Data Format\n",
    "\n",
    "The dataset consists of two files.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### File 1: HDF5\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "berlin-apc.h5\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Contains:\n",
    "\n",
    "* All image sequences\n",
    "* Float16 arrays\n",
    "* Pixel values normalized between 0 and 1\n",
    "\n",
    "Size:\n",
    "\n",
    "Approximately 2.3–2.4 GB.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### File 2: CSV Labels\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "berlin-apc.csv\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Contains:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Column        | Meaning         |\n",
    "| ------------- | --------------- |\n",
    "| sequence_name | Identifier      |\n",
    "| boarding      | Number entering |\n",
    "| alighting     | Number leaving  |\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "| sequence | boarding | alighting |\n",
    "| -------- | -------- | --------- |\n",
    "| seq001   | 4        | 2         |\n",
    "| seq002   | 0        | 3         |\n",
    "| seq003   | 1        | 0         |\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Annotation Process\n",
    "\n",
    "Creating labels was extremely labor-intensive.\n",
    "\n",
    "Each sequence was:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Viewed by multiple human annotators\n",
    "2. Counted independently\n",
    "3. Compared against other annotators\n",
    "\n",
    "If disagreement occurred:\n",
    "\n",
    "* More reviewers were assigned\n",
    "* Up to seven reviewers examined difficult sequences\n",
    "\n",
    "Only after consensus was reached were labels accepted. \n",
    "\n",
    "#### Quality Control\n",
    "\n",
    "Researchers removed sequences that:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Had severe sensor failures\n",
    "* Were impossible to interpret\n",
    "* Were marked undecidable by multiple annotators\n",
    "\n",
    "This improved dataset reliability. \n",
    "\n",
    "#### Privacy Features\n",
    "\n",
    "The dataset is called **privacy-friendly** because:\n",
    "\n",
    "* No RGB Images: No visible photographs.\n",
    "* No Faces: Face recognition impossible.\n",
    "* No Clothing Details: Cannot identify individuals.\n",
    "* No Biometric Information: No personal characteristics visible.\n",
    "* Only Depth Maps: Distance measurements only.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Typical Challenges in the Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "The dataset contains many difficult real-world situations:\n",
    "\n",
    "### Dense Crowds: Multiple passengers crossing simultaneously.\n",
    "\n",
    "* Bicycles: Passengers carrying bicycles.\n",
    "* Large Objects: Luggage and bulky items.\n",
    "* Occlusions: One passenger blocking another.\n",
    "* Sensor Noise: Depth measurement errors.\n",
    "* Long Sequences: Extended station dwell times.\n",
    "* Empty Door Openings: Doors opening without passenger movement.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Label Definition\n",
    "\n",
    "Each sequence has two target values.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Boarding Count\n",
    "\n",
    "Number of passengers entering train.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "5\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "means 5 people boarded.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Alighting Count\n",
    "\n",
    "Number of passengers leaving train.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "3\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "means 3 people exited.\n",
    "\n",
    "Thus label:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "(5,3)\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "means:\n",
    "\n",
    "* 5 entered\n",
    "* 3 exited\n",
    "\n",
    "during the same door opening.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why the Dataset Is Important\n",
    "\n",
    "Before Berlin-APC:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Most APC datasets were private.\n",
    "* Public APC benchmarks were scarce.\n",
    "* Privacy-compliant APC research was difficult.\n",
    "\n",
    "Berlin-APC became one of the first large-scale open datasets enabling reproducible APC research. \n",
    "\n",
    "### Machine Learning Tasks Enabled\n",
    "\n",
    "Researchers can use the dataset for:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Passenger Counting: Estimate number entering and leaving.\n",
    "* Regression: Predict counts directly.\n",
    "* Sequence Modeling: Analyze temporal passenger movement.\n",
    "* Event Detection: Detect entry/exit events.\n",
    "* Crowd Analysis: Understand flow patterns.\n",
    "* Edge AI: Develop models for embedded devices.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Baseline Research: NAPC\n",
    "\n",
    "The dataset was used to develop: NAPC\n",
    "\n",
    "NAPC is an end-to-end neural network based on:\n",
    "\n",
    "* LSTM architecture\n",
    "* Sequence learning\n",
    "* Direct prediction of boarding and alighting counts\n",
    "\n",
    "The model processes variable-length depth-video sequences and outputs two numbers:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Boarding count\n",
    "Alighting count\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "without explicit person detection or tracking. \n",
    "\n",
    "### Advantages of Berlin-APC\n",
    "\n",
    "* Publicly Available: Researchers worldwide can access it.\n",
    "* Large Scale: Nearly 13,000 sequences.\n",
    "* Real-World Data: Collected during actual train operations.\n",
    "* Privacy Preserving: No identifiable passengers.\n",
    "* Expert Labels: Multi-stage human verification.\n",
    "* Variable-Length Sequences: Reflects realistic operations.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "### Limitations\n",
    "\n",
    "* Single Sensor Type: Only depth information.\n",
    "* Single Environment: Regional trains around Berlin.\n",
    "* Low Resolution: 20×25 may limit advanced vision methods.\n",
    "* No Identity Tracking: Cannot study individual trajectories.\n",
    "* No RGB Data: Appearance-based methods impossible.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Dataset Statistics Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "| Property            | Value                           |                                 \n",
    "| ------------------- | ------------------------------- | \n",
    "| Purpose             | Automated Passenger Counting    |                                 \n",
