    "**Berlin-APC is a large-scale, publicly available, privacy-preserving dataset of 12,956 low-resolution 3D LiDAR train-door video sequences, annotated with boarding and alighting passenger counts, specifically created to develop and evaluate AI-based automated passenger counting systems without exposing passenger identities.** \n",
